<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Join</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <i style="font-style:normal; font-weight:bold;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Polylines &gt; Join</b></span></i> <span lang="EN-GB">or by pressing</span> <span class="Shortcut" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Shift + J</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Join</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command merges two visible polylines into a single one by connecting the end points of both polylines. The ends to be joined are selected using the mouse. The join will be a straight line.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">When this command is called the mouse pointer changes to cross with number showing the current point for selecting.</span><span lang="EN-GB">&#160;</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="processing_polylines_files/image035.gif" width="32px" height="32px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt="">&#160;&#160;&#160; <img src="processing_polylines_files/image036.gif" width="32px" height="32px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt="">&#160;&#160;&#160; Mouse pointers in</span> <span class="Mode">Join</span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Using the cursor, click on the two points to be joined together. While in this mode you can rotate the viewport using</span> <b style="font-weight:normal;"><span class="Shortcut">Shift + left mouse button</span></b><span lang="EN-GB">, pan using</span> <b style="font-weight:normal;"><span class="Shortcut">Shift + right mouse button</span></b><span lang="EN-GB">, and zoom using</span> <b style="font-weight:normal;"><span class="Shortcut">Shift + middle mouse button</span></b> <span lang="EN-GB">or the mouse wheel.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP225514636" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<table cellspacing="5" class="whs5">
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs6">
<td class="whs7">
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="processing_polylines_files/image038.jpg" width="329px" height="164px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td class="whs9">
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="processing_polylines_files/image040.jpg" width="329px" height="164px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</div>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Exit this mode by switching to another one –</span> <span class="Mode">Zoom Window</span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> <span class="Mode">Zoom Mode</span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> <span class="Mode">Rotate</span><span lang="EN-GB">, or</span> <span class="Mode">Pan</span><span lang="EN-GB">. This mode is not stored so when you open another window,</span> <span class="Mode">Zoom Window</span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode will be enabled.</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="p1"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">: The first node of the merged polyline will coincide with that first node, which was not used for joining. So the sequence of connecting two points is not important. See</span> <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span class="Command" style="text-decoration:none;">Draw First Point</span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">command from the</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>View</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">menu for details about displaying first nodes. You can revert the direction of a particular polyline using the</span> <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span class="Command">Reverse Order</span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">command.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="color:#ff0000; text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP225705961" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<table cellspacing="5" class="whs5">
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs6">
<td class="whs7">
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="processing_polylines_files/image043.jpg" width="330px" height="168px" border="0" class="img_whs10" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td class="whs9">
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="processing_polylines_files/image045.jpg" width="330px" height="167px" border="0" class="img_whs11" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB">It is the same whether you will first pick point A or point B (first nodes are displayed as yellow squares)</span></p>
</div>
